  "version": "0.1.0",
  "notes": "First preview of Aether DV, a D-RATS-compatible D-STAR data application.\n\n**Tested in simulation only.** No interoperability tests with real D-RATS stations, and no tests on real radios or over the air, have been done yet. Use it alongside D-RATS, not instead of it.\n\nWhat's in it:\n- **Engine (`aetherd`)**\n  - Ports: serial radio ports and ratflector connections.\n  - Legacy D-RATS behaviour: chat, ping, version query, file and form transfer.\n  - ICS-213 messages, and position reports (NMEA and DPRS).\n  - Diagnostics: wire capture (`.aecap`) and support bundles.\n- **Desktop app**\n  - Views: Chat, Messages (ICS-213), Transfers, Stations and Diagnostics.\n  - Radio Setup: step-by-step setup per brand and model, with links. Guides start from manuals only and are updated from operators' reports.\n  - Sounds: an optional sound for each kind of event, each switchable.\n  - Engine: it can start the bundled engine with your configuration file.\n  - Updates: \"Check for updates\" is in Diagnostics; updates install only when you click Install.\n- **Command line:** `aether-cli`, and `aether-bench` for scripted interop runs.\n- **CI-V:** checks that the radio's DV Fast Data setting matches the port (IC-9700, ID-52 PLUS).\n\nKnown limits:\n- Installers are not code-signed for Windows or notarised for macOS. Expect a security warning on first install.\n- macOS builds are for Apple silicon only.\n- No map, settings screen or file picker yet. Ports are set up in the configuration file (see `examples/` in the source).",
  "pub_date": "2026-10-30T12:25:10Z",
